{"author":{"id":"e8ccbc170af88335916e23a1b24e48c04b0a4af82e988d5245cc91e39d6a9e2c"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794491102,"nonce":"/R7qnQq6aPajYEoLz5f3QlxfEDI=","title":"L2 — Python Scrapling sidecar for Mercado Libre UY and TEMU","message":"## Context\nScraping uses the original Python Scrapling, run by `uv` as a long-lived process that talks JSON lines over stdin/stdout. This layer is plan Task 4 (`docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-12-maeve.md:183`).\n\n## Files\n- `scraper/` — new uv project: `pyproject.toml`, `maeve_scraper/{__main__,protocol,parse}.py`, `maeve_scraper/sites/{mercadolibre,temu}.py`, `tests/`\n- `tests/fixtures/{ml_item.html,temu_item.html}` — real pages, captured once with `StealthyFetcher`\n\n## Approach\n- Follow plan Task 4 steps and protocol exactly (request `{id,url}`, `{\"ready\":true}` on start, `ok`/`error.kind` responses, product JSON = L1 `Product` serde)\n- ML: JSON-LD first, then the Características table, review text capped at 20. TEMU: embedded page JSON first, resolve `share.temu.com` redirects, reviews optional (cap 10)\n- Variants: use the price of the variant selected in the URL; otherwise the lowest price with `price_is_range: true`\n- Confirm the Scrapling API names against its README before coding\n\n## Depends on\nL1 — `Product` JSON shape\n\n## Out of scope\n- Rust client (L3)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- `parse_price` tests from plan Task 4 Step 3 pass, including `\"U$S 49,90\"` → `(4990,\"USD\")` and `\"$ 1.234\"` → `(123400,\"UYU\")` (Review Focus 1)\n- Fixture tests assert concrete title, price and specs read from each saved page\n- Unsupported host → `kind: \"unsupported\"`; a malformed line does not kill the loop\n- `scraper-tests` gate passes; read the count of tests RUN, not the exit code\n- Manual: piping a real ML UY URL into `uv run python -m maeve_scraper` returns a product","files":null}]}